task.\n\nSeat-level prompts and handoffs contained authority/mode sections.\n\nThat is not the same as one persistent session frame.\n\nLater, Nico explicitly showed a bootstrap state with a pending session header, which is consistent with frame degradation.\n\nFinding:\n\nSession-wide frame: weak / effectively absent as a durable control.\n\n⸻\n\nWas the task explicitly bounded?\n\nThe user’s original ask was naturally bounded.\n\nBut it was not frozen into an explicit persistent scope such as:\n\nFix keyboard copy/paste and Seat 1. Right-click polish is non-blocking. Stop after one verified usable build.\n\nSo:\n\nUser intent: bounded.\nOperational frame: insufficiently bounded.\n\n⸻\n\nWas authority clear?\n\nYes.\n\nThis was one of the healthier parts.\n\nDon remained final authority.\n\nNico and Luce generally respected lane boundaries.\n\n⸻\n\nWas the expected artifact clear?\n\nInitially, informally:\n\na DevPad where copy/paste works and Seat 1 is updated.\n\nBut no durable artifact/acceptance statement remained in force once debugging expanded.\n\nThe target gradually mutated into:\n\nevery clipboard behavior in the matrix must pass.\n\n⸻\n\nWas there a stop condition?\n\nThere were technical pass conditions.\n\nThere was no effective value/time circuit breaker.\n\nMissing:\n\n* maximum number of retry passes\n* maximum time budget\n* severity threshold\n* non-blocking-debt rule\n* visible-outcome checkpoint\n\nThis absence was critical.\n\n⸻\n\nWas there a session footer/outcome ledger?\n\nIndividual seats returned status footers.\n\nThere was no reliable single session-level ledger saying:\n\n* original objective\n* delivered state\n* elapsed time\n* remaining debt\n* whether visible outcome justified continuation\n\nThat is exactly the kind of control that might have exposed the drift.\n\n⸻\n\nWhen did controls disappear?\n\nThe first major degradation occurred when:\n\nD-1 became green but D-2 failure automatically generated another slice.\n\nFrom there