", "text"], "text": "Make sure to include fileciteturn0file0L5-L8 in your response to cite this file, or to surface it as a link. Replace the placeholder line range with the actual line range from the result that best fits the snippet you want to surface with the citation. If you cite multiple files, use a separate complete `filecite` marker for each file. Never put multiple `turnNfileM` targets inside a single `filecite` marker.\nUse ref_id \"turn0file0\" to reference this file. For broad questions or unknown locations, retrieve relevant chunks with `files.search` scoped to this file. Use `files.find` only for exact text, and use `files.read` for a known range or to expand relevant results. Full file size: 1148 file lines.\n[L1] # GCE SESSION POSTMORTEM — LOOP / FRAME DRIFT RECON\n\n[L3] **AUTHORITY:** Don\n[L4] **MODE:** READ-ONLY POSTMORTEM\n[L5] **SCOPE:** This chat, reconstructed from the first substantive Drive/Cable Car work through the OAuth setup point.\n[L6] **NO BUILD ACTIONS TAKEN.**\n\n[L8] One framing point matters immediately: this chat actually contained **two sequential workstreams**. The first was Google Drive cleanup/reconciliation. The second was Cable Car architecture/build. The Drive cleanup was comparatively clean. Most of the loop characteristics appeared after Don said, essentially, **“you own the architecture and methodology; let’s spec it to build with Nico.”**\n\n---\n\n[L12] # A. ORIGINAL ASK\n\n[L14] There were two actual asks.\n\n[L16] ### Phase 1 — Drive cleanup\n\n[L18] Don wanted the Google Drive estate cleaned up and reconciled so that its structure reflected the local GCE authority model closely enough that paths were understandable and durable.\n\n[L20] The requested outcome was essentially:\n\n[L22] > Clean the existing Drive, preserve valid current/historical material, and organize the GCE portion so its authority/routing logic resembles `GCE_ORG / GCE_IDENTITY / Projects / GCE_DON`.\n\n[L24] That was accomplished.\n\n[L26]