ive DevPad execution request forward.\n[L6] **FINDING:** The session produced substantial valid software, but later entered a **process/architecture loop around canonical Model Synthesis integration**.\n\n---\n\n[L10] ## A. ORIGINAL ASK\n\n[L12] The first real implementation objective was materially smaller than where the session ended.\n\n[L14] Don wanted the **Edge Crew Quant DevPad made visible and usable in React**, starting with a narrow vertical slice:\n\n[L16] **Frozen MLB state → React DevPad → MLB slate → one game → Baseline → drill-down/evidence/provenance.**\n\n[L18] The requested product outcome was essentially:\n\n[L20] > **Let me see the Quant machine operating in the DevPad instead of reading terminal/state dumps.**\n\n[L22] The original first-slice scope did **not** require, at that moment:\n\n[L24] - canonical MLB human-input-to-numeric synthesis semantics;\n[L25] - a new value-materialization architecture;\n[L26] - successor MLB manifest design;\n[L27] - canonical `ecq-synthesis-v1` registration;\n[L28] - multiple architecture gates around synthesis;\n[L29] - a new FixedDec value contract;\n[L30] - exhaustive cross-seat certification of every later layer.\n\n[L32] Those entered later.\n\n---\n\n[L36] # B. EXPECTED SIZE OF WORK\n\n[L38] ### Classification: **NORMAL BUILD**\n\n[L40] It was larger than bounded maintenance because there was no current React web surface on disk and a new vertical slice had to be assembled.\n\n[L42] It was **not initially an architecture-change request** because Gate 6 architecture and Parent Quant methodology already existed and the intended first pass explicitly fit inside them.\n\n[L44] A sane estimate of the original work shape was:\n\n[L46] **inspect existing repo → build adapter/contracts/API projection → React view → tests → show Don.**\n\n[L48] The first slice legitimately required engineering discipline, but it did **not** require repeated governance expansion.\n\n---\n\n[L52] # C. ACTUAL WORK PERFORMED\n\n[L54] Only concrete built/tested outcomes are counted here.\n\n[L56] ### 1. React DevPad / Baseline slice — genuinely built\n\n[L58] A Vite/React/TypeScript DevPad was created over the frozen MLB fixture.\n\n[L60] It materially provided:\n\n[L62] - 12-game MLB PREGAME slate;\n[L63] - event selection;\n[L64] - separate BASELINE view;\n[L65] - component/evidence drill-down;\n[L66] - provenance;\n[L67] - uncertainty/evidence state;\n[L68] - generic sport-module boundary;\n[L69] - immutable Baseline;\n[L70] - deterministic state identity;\n[L71] - injected clock;\n[L72] - read-only enforcement.\n\n[L74] This was a **real visible product outcome**.\n\n[L76] ### 2. SHA-256 defect — genuinely found and fixed\n\n[L78] Initial implementation contained a broken custom SHA-256 padding calculation.\n\n[L80] Luce correctly found that hashes labeled SHA-256 did not match standards.\n\n[L82] Nico/Big Pickle then actually repaired:\n\n[L84] - SHA-256 padding;\n[L85] - fixed-vector tests;\n[L86] - Node crypto cross-checks;\n[L87] - derived state identity;\n[L88] - browser compatibility;\n[L89] - app→test dependency.\n\n[L91] Result reached:\n\n[L93] **37/37 tests + clean build.**\n\n[L95] This was valid corrective work.\n\n[L97] ### 3. Don Delta — genuinely built\n\n[L99] A second independently addressable view was implemented:\n\n[L101] **Human input → classification → validation → Don Delta.**\n\n[L103] Actual implementation included:\n\n[L105] - immutable human input records;\n[L106] - classification surface;\n[L107] - validation state;\n[L108] - append-only Don Delta ledger;\n[L109] - supersession;\n[L110] - write authority;\n[L111] - anti-lookahead;\n[L112] - deterministic replay;\n[L113] - React Don Delta UI;\n[L114] - three-view routing.\n\n[L116] Result eventually reached:\n\n[L118] **73/73 tests.**\n\n[L120] ### 4. Clock/vocabulary repair — genuinely implemented\n\n[L122] The Don Delta implementation was revised so that:\n\n[L124] - `RunClock` pinned a declared run instant;\n[L125] - authoritative writes stopped depending on accidental execution-time variance;\n[L126] - validation became:\n[L127]   `UNVALIDATED / VALIDATED / REFUTED / EXPIRED`;\n[L128] - verification became the orthogonal:\n[L129]   `FULL / PARTIAL / UNVERIFIABLE`;\n[L130] - Don Delta envelope was versioned appropriately.\n\n[L132] Result reached:\n\n[L134] **94/94 tests.**\n\n[L136] ### 5. Generic Model Synthesis shell — genuinely built\n\n[L138] The third state was materially implemented as generic infrastructure:\n\n[L140] - Model Synthesis envelope;\n[L141] - deterministic identity;\n[L142] - exact Baseline lineage;\n[L143] - exact Don Delta lineage;\n[L144] - append-only synthesis history;\n[L145] - write authority;\n[L146] - replay;\n[L147] - anti-lookahead;\n[L148] - React Model Synthesis view;\n[L149] - NON-CANON transcript transform;\n[L150] - loud failure when the canonical MLB transform did not exist.\n\n[L152] This was another **real visible product outcome**.\n\n[L154] Result reached:\n\n[L156] **114/114 tests + clean build.**\n\n[L158] ### 6. Canonical MLB synthesis math core — genuinely built\n\n[L160] Corrado defined enough MLB numeric semantics for Nico to implement a pure math core.\n\n[L162] Nico actually implemented:\n\n[L164] `mlb_ecq_synthesis_v1.ts`\n\n[L166] including:\n\n[L168] - additive `M_delta`;\n[L169] - per-variable bounds;\n[L170] - ±0.10 total cap;\n[L171] - 0.05/0.95 probability clamp;\n[L172] - complement conservation;\n[L173] - 6dp integer/micro-unit arithmetic;\n[L174] - no interactions;\n[L175] - lane gating.\n\n[L177] Tests eventually reached:\n\n[L179] **127/127**, then **129/129** after lane-map correction.\n\n[L181] ### 7. Lane-map defect — genuinely fixed\n\n[L183] Luce found:\n\n[L185] - MONEYLINE incorrectly admitted weather/park/umpire;\n[L186] - TOTALS `days_rest` required a semantic ruling.\n\n[L188] Corrado ruled TOTALS excludes `days_rest`.\n\n[L190] Nico corrected the lane sets and added regression tests.\n\n[L192] Luce independently reverified:\n\n[L194] - MONEYLINE 5 families;\n[L195] - TOTALS 7;\n[L196] - RUNLINE 5;\n[L197] - 129/129 green.\n\n[L199] This was valid engineering correction.\n\n[L201] ### 8. Value-materialization architecture — **not yet built**\n\n[L203] At session end, Chiave had frozen a proposed value-materialization contract.\n\n[L205] But the actual new layer was **not yet implemented**.\n\n[L207] Therefore it is not a completed deliverable.\n\n---\n\n[L211] # D. LOOP ONSET\n\n[L213] There are two useful boundaries.\n\n[L215] ### Product-scope drift began after the original first slice\n\n[L217] Once the Baseline React DevPad existed and was verified, the original visible outcome had been achieved.\n\n[L219] Moving to Don Delta was an **explicitly authorized expansion by Don**, so I would **not** call that alone the loop.\n\n[L221] ### Actual loop onset: after the generic Model Synthesis shell was working\n\n[L223] The strongest loop onset is when the session moved from:\n\n[L225] > **“Model Synthesis shell exists and correctly fails loudly because canonical MLB synthesis semantics are absent.”**\n\nto:\n\n[L229] > **“Now let's make canonical `ecq-synthesis-v1@1.0.0` executable inside this same DevPad session.”**\n\n[L231] That decision converted a successful product-build session into a methodology + architecture + contract-reconciliation program.\n\n[L233] At that point the shell itself had already proven the boundary correctly: **SPORT GAP → Corrado**.\n\n[L235] Instead of closing the DevPad build at that visible checkpoint, the session continued into:\n\n[L237] Corrado semantics → Nico math core → Luce → lane correction → Corrado → Nico → Luce → Chiave → Corrado value materialization → Chiave new contract freeze.\n\n[L239] That is the clearest loop branch.\n\n---\n\n[L243] # E. LOOP MECHANISM\n\n[L245] The loop became:\n\n[L247] **Don → Coda framing → Nico → Luce → Coda → next layer → Nico → Luce → Coda → specialty seat → Nico → Luce → architecture gate → new contract → next implementation.**\n\n[L249] More specifically:\n\n[L251] ### Phase 1 — Healthy\n\n[L253] **Coda → Nico → Luce**\n\n[L255] Baseline React slice.\n\n[L257] Luce found a real SHA problem.\n\n[L259] **Nico fix → Luce reverify.**\n\n[L261] This was normal build/verify/fix.\n\n[L263] ### Phase 2 — Still productive, but expanding\n\n[L265] **Don authorizes Don Delta → Nico → Luce.**\n\n[L267] Luce finds clock/vocabulary issues.\n\n[L269] Instead of treating this as one bounded closure patch, orchestration added:\n\n[L271] - pre-Slice-3 reconciliation;\n[L272] - special Nico grounding;\n[L273] - Coda reconciliation;\n[L274] - separate repair verification;\n[L275] - final Coda reconciliation.\n\n[L277] Useful work occurred, but process started expanding around the work.\n\n[L279] ### Phase 3 — Generic Model Synthesis\n\n[L281] **Don → Nico → Luce.**\n\n[L283] Again productive. A visible third view existed.\n\n[L285] But then the shell's intentionally loud missing-transform condition became the next project.\n\n[L287] ### Phase 4 — Recursive semantic integration\n\n[L289] **Coda → Corrado**\n[L290] defines canonical MLB synthesis.\n\n[L292] Corrado reports undefined semantics.\n\n[L294] **Don/Coda ruling → Nico**\n[L295] builds math core.\n\n[L297] **Luce**\n[L298] finds lane-map issue.\n\n[L300] **Corrado**\n[L301] rules TOTALS/rest.\n\n[L303] **Nico**\n[L304] patches.\n\n[L306] **Luce**\n[L307] reverifies.\n\n[L309] At this point the math core is valid, but still not runnable through the shell.\n\n[L311] ### Phase 5 — Architecture recursion\n\n[L313] **Chiave**\n[L314] reviews shell registration.\n\n[L316] Chiave correctly refuses because the shell has references but there is **no certified producer for numeric delta magnitudes**.\n\n[L318] This is the most important evidence that the session had outrun its original operating frame.\n\n[L320] The missing thing was no longer \"one code fix.\"\n\n[L322] It was:\n\n[L324] > **There is no authoritative human-read → quantitative-value layer.**\n\nThen:\n\n[L328] **Coda → Corrado**\n[L329] defines value materialization.\n\n[L331] Corrado discovers human utterance → numeric magnitude is itself undefined.\n\n[L333] **Coda/Don**\n[L334] rules explicit magnitude only.\n\n[L336] **Chiave**\n[L337] freezes an entirely new `ecq-value-materialization@1.0.0` contract.\n\n[L339] That is effectively a **new subsystem** born inside the same DevPad session.\n\n---\n\n[L343] ## Specific loop behaviors\n\n[L345] ### Minor issue became new slice/pass\n\n[L347] The clock/vocabulary repair after Slice 2 became a distinct pre-Slice-3 gate rather than a bounded Slice-2 closure patch.\n\n[L349] ### Verifier became design influence\n\n[L351] Luce did not improperly design, but findings repeatedly became the **trigger for the next architecture/governance branch**.\n\n[L353] Examples:\n\n[L355] - SHA defect → appropriate fix.\n[L356] - SystemClock observation → dedicated reconciliation layer.\n[L357] - validation vocabulary → contract migration.\n[L358] - lane-map mismatch → specialty-seat reroute.\n[L359] - shell references-only evidence → architecture gate.\n\n[L361] The problem was not Luce finding them; the problem was orchestration repeatedly turning findings into **new lifecycle stages**.\n\n[L363] ### Coda inferred or extended architecture\n\n[L365] The largest example was proposing a separate `SynthesisOverlayValueSet` / value-materialization layer before Chiave's formal freeze.\n\n[L367] That idea turned out to be sensible, but it was nevertheless a **new architectural object introduced while the original DevPad session was still open**.\n\n[L369] ### Builder interruption\n\n[L371] Dots3 was interrupted and replaced by Big Pickle due to repeated stalls.\n\n[L373] Later Nico's work was repeatedly stopped at semantic seams and handed to:\n\n[L375] Corrado → Luce → Chiave → Corrado → Chiave.\n\n[L377] Those later interruptions were often justified by authority boundaries, but they prevented a single coherent \"build → show → close\" rhythm.\n\n[L379] ### Same question effectively answered repeatedly\n\n[L381] Examples:\n\n[L383] - \"Is Slice 1 done?\" answered by builder, then Luce, then Coda.\n[L384] - \"Is Slice 2 ready?\" builder → Luce → pre-Slice-3 repair → Luce → Coda.\n[L385] - \"Is Model Synthesis ready?\" shell implementation → Luce → Corrado → math implementation → Luce → lane fix → Luce → Chiave.\n[L386] - \"Can canonical synthesis execute?\" repeatedly approached from shell, methodology, math core, lane maps, then value surface.\n\n[L388] ### Confidence decreased despite more work\n\n[L390] A major example:\n\n[L392] Generic Model Synthesis shell was green and honest.\n\n[L394] Then pursuing canonical execution exposed that the state model did **not actually contain executable human delta magnitudes**.\n\n[L396] So after more work, the system knew more—but the path to canonical registration became **less complete than initially assumed**.\n\n[L398] That is a classic sign of scope outrunning ground truth.\n\n[L400] ### Certification replaced visible progress\n\n[L402] The period after the Model Synthesis shell became visible produced many:\n\n[L404] - handoffs;\n[L405] - test counts;\n[L406] - rulings;\n[L407] - gate verdicts;\n[L408] - semantic definitions;\n[L409] - re-verifications;\n\n[L411] but **no corresponding new end-user capability appeared in the React DevPad**.\n\n---\n\n[L415] # F. ASSUMPTIONS / INVENTED STATE\n\n[L417] | ClaimClassificationFinding                                             |                                            |                                                                         |\n[L418] | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n[L419] | Frozen MLB data could drive a React Baseline surface                   | **VERIFIED**                         