n while asleep).\nNEXT ROUTE:     Hold with Luce until Don reports an event.\nTo use it — use Space Bunny normally. The moment it stalls or disconnects, run:\npowershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File \"C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\Desktop\\GCE_LUCE_TELEMETRY\\mark.ps1\" -Note \"stall while doing X\"\nThat stamps the exact timestamp into the CSV within 10 s. Then just tell me it happened — I'll read the telemetry around the mark and return the verdict.\nTo check at any time: read.ps1 · To end the test: stop.ps1\nI am not inferring anything from this clean window. Waiting on your event.", "text_chars": 2622, "code_blocks": 0, "links": ["https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1"], "citations": ["https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1"], "path_references": ["Brother\\Desktop\\GCE_LUCE_TELEMETRY\\mark.ps1", "C:\\Users\\Dekan", "events.log", "mark.ps1", "monitor.ps1", "read.ps1", "stop.ps1", "telemetry.csv"], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "a8b89338-eea4-4e0d-aa45-8d7fbb69a955", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790373190.318711, "updated_at": 1790373190.318711, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "06c36a3e-3f42-4603-8381-cd7b7fee0482", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790373190.321103, "updated_at": 1790373199.3454, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════  \n**GCE — LUCE NETWORK CORRELATION HOLD**  \n**AUTHORITY:** Don | **PRIMARY SEAT:** Coda | **OWNER:** Luce  \n**MODE:** QUICK VERIFICATION  \n**CONFIDENCE:** **99%**  \n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nPerfect. **This is exactly where we should stop touching it.**\n\nLuce has done the right thing:\n\n- instrumentation is live;\n- all three probes are verified;\n- Bedrock Mantle endpoint was read from config, not guessed;\n- the false first-hop readings were caught as a **monitor bug**, discarded, and restarted clean;\n- blind spots are explicitly documented;\n- no root-cause claim is being made before a real event.\n\nSo there is **nothing else to investigate right now**.\n\nUse Space Bunny normally. The next time it stalls, run the existing `mark.ps1` once with a short note. Then bring me the Luce readout around that timestamp.\n\nAt that point we should be able to separate:\n\n**A. Network-correlated**  \nFirst hop / Internet / provider TCP degrade at the same time.\n\n**B. Network-not-correlated**  \nThose remain clean while Space Bunny stalls → move directly into **OpenCode / Bedrock Mantle / provider streaming / client-runtime** investigation.\n\n**C. Ambiguous**  \nVery short event or local-radio issue invisible to the current 10-second probes → then we tighten only that measurement, not rebuild the whole diagnostic stack.\n\nAnd importantly: **do not add more scripts now.** We finally have one working monitor. Let the failure come to the instrumentation.\n\n---\n\n**CURRENT MODE:** Quick verification  \n**OWNER:** Luce  \n**STATUS:** Monitor armed / waiting for real event  \n**VERDICT:** INCONCLUSIVE by design  \n**NEXT:** Mark one actual Space Bunny stall and correlate telemetry  \n**CONFIDENCE:** 99% on current process state", "text_chars": 1830, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": ["mark.ps1"], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "00e8e03e-3346-4f82-a4e2-647701655680", "role": "user", "role_na